    title: "Crochet Caterpillar Amigurumi Pattern: Colorful Worm with Round Balls & Little Legs (PDF)",
    description: "Crochet a charming rainbow caterpillar with this step-by-step amigurumi pattern! The worm is made of soft, round, colorful balls with little grey legs, a sweet smiling face, big eyes, and two cute antennae. The head stands about 17 cm (6.7 in) tall, and you choose how many balls to make, so you can crochet a short worm or a long, snuggly one.",
    patternText: `<h1>Worm Pattern - Large Pieces</h1><p><strong>Abbreviations:</strong> MR magic ring, sc single crochet, inc increase, dec decrease, hdc half double crochet, FLO front loop only. *...* repeat only what is between asterisks.</p><section><h2>Body - Large Piece</h2><p>Pink cotton thread, 2.5 mm hook.</p><ul><li>1) 6 sc in MR. (6)</li><li>2) 6 inc. (12)</li><li>3-7) 1 sc around. (12)</li><li>8) 1 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (18)</li><li>9) FLO, 2 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (24)</li><li>10) 3 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (30)</li><li>11) 4 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (36)</li><li>12) 5 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (42)</li><li>13) 6 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (48)</li><li>14) 7 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (54)</li><li>15-25) 1 sc around. (54)</li><li>26) 7 sc, 1 dec, 6 times. (48)</li><li>27) 6 sc, 1 dec, 6 times. (42)</li><li>28) 5 sc, 1 dec, 6 times. (36)</li><li>29) 4 sc, 1 dec, 6 times. (30)</li><li>30) 3 sc, 1 dec, 6 times. (24)</li><li>31) 2 sc, 1 dec, 6 times. (18)</li></ul><p>Cut the thread and fill the ball.</p></section><section><h2>Tail - Large Piece</h2><p>Orange cotton thread, 2.5 mm hook.</p><ul><li>1) 6 sc in MR. (6)</li><li>2) 6 inc. (12)</li><li>3) 1 sc around. (12)</li><li>4) 1 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (18)</li><li>5) 2 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (24)</li><li>6) 3 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (30)</li><li>7) 4 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (36)</li><li>8) 5 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (42)</li><li>9-16) 1 sc around. (42)</li><li>17) 5 sc, 1 dec, 6 times. (36)</li><li>18) 4 sc, 1 dec, 6 times. (30)</li><li>19) 3 sc, 1 dec, 6 times. (24)</li><li>20) 2 sc, 1 dec, 6 times. (18)</li></ul><p>Cut the thread. Fill.</p><p><em>Note: The original PDF prints the plain-round range as 8-16; it is written here as 9-16 because row 8 is an increase round.</em></p></section><section><h2>Neck - Large Piece</h2><p>Green cotton thread, 2.5 mm hook.</p><ul><li>1) 6 sc in MR. (6)</li><li>2) 6 inc. (12)</li><li>3) 1 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (18)</li><li>4) 2 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (24)</li><li>5) 3 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (30)</li><li>6) 4 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (36)</li><li>7) 5 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (42)</li><li>8) 6 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (48)</li><li>9-18) 1 sc around. (54)</li><li>19) 6 sc, 1 dec, 6 times. (42)</li><li>20) 5 sc, 1 dec, 6 times. (36)</li><li>21) 4 sc, 1 dec, 6 times. (30)</li><li>22) 3 sc, 1 dec, 6 times. (24)</li><li>23) 2 sc, 1 dec, 6 times. (18)</li></ul><p>Cut the thread and fill.</p><p><em>Note: Copied as printed in the original. Row 8 ends with 48 stitches but rows 9-18 are listed as 54, so check the count there (an increase round of 7 sc, 1 inc x 6 would bridge 48 to 54).</em></p></section><section><h2>Head - Large Piece</h2><p>Green cotton thread, 2.5 mm hook.</p><ul><li>1) 6 sc in MR. (6)</li><li>2) 6 inc. (12)</li><li>3) 1 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (18)</li><li>4) 2 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (24)</li><li>5) 3 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (30)</li><li>6) 4 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (36)</li><li>7) 5 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (42)</li><li>8) 6 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (48)</li><li>9) 7 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (54)</li><li>10) 8 sc, 1 inc, 6 times. (60)</li><li>11-17) 1 sc around. (60)</li><li>18) 2 hdc inc, 18 sc, 2 hdc inc, 38 sc. (64)</li><li>19) *1 hdc, 1 hdc inc* 2 times, 18 sc, *1 hdc inc, 1 hdc* 2 times, 38 sc. (68)</li><li>20-21) 1 sc around. (68)</li><li>22) *1 hdc, 1 hdc dec* 2 times, 18 sc, *1 hdc dec, 1 hdc* 2 times, 38 sc. (64)</li><li>23) 2 hdc dec, 18 sc, 2 hdc dec. (60)</li><li>24) *8 sc, 1 dec* 6 times. (54)</li><li>25) *7 sc, 1 dec* 6 times. (48)</li><li>26) *6 sc, 1 dec* 6 times. (42)</li><li>27) *5 sc, 1 dec* 6 times. (36)</li><li>28) *4 sc, 1 dec* 6 times. (30)</li><li>29) *3 sc, 1 dec* 6 times. (24)</li><li>30) *2 sc, 1 dec* 6 times. (18)</li></ul><p>Cut the thread and fill.</p></section>`,
